meta {
  name: 5 Subscribe to provider
  type: http
  seq: 5
}
post {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{customerEmail}}/subscriptions/{{providerEmail}}
  body: none
}
docs {
  Idempotent: subscribing twice is still `202 Accepted` and does not duplicate the entry
  (`$addToSet`). Writes both sides of the relationship — the customer's
  `subscribedProviderCollection` and the provider's own `subscribedCustomerCollection` — so a
  provider's own "my subscribers" view (not yet built) can read the same write.

  `{{customerEmail}}` in the path must match the caller's own `sub` claim — a customer can only
  manage their own subscriptions (`403` otherwise). `404` if `{{providerEmail}}` matches no provider.
}
